  "hypotheses": [
    "Retryable outcomes (503, 429 and 408, an exchange timeout and a transport failure) are retried within the attempt budget. Every scheduled delay is reported with its attempt ordinal and drawn from the injected jitter source, and each occurrence ends acknowledged, or reported exhausted with an exhaustion alert.",
    "A permanent 4xx and a malformed acknowledgment stop retrying at once and are reported: the 4xx as a rejection, the malformed acknowledgment as an unknown outcome although the collector stored the occurrence.",
    "A lost acknowledgment, and a timeout after ingest, are redelivered byte-identical; the collector acknowledges the redelivery as a duplicate and stores the occurrence once.",
    "Every planned occurrence ends in exactly one terminal bucket, with expected losses in the denominator and none unexplained, at small volume and at volume."
